honest . . . they don't really appear to fit any of the core eras. And it seems like they'd be occupying the same &quot;space&quot; as other factions: Project Utopia (the ties to the UN) and the Directive (the espionage angle), for example<br /> <br /> On the other hand, &quot;Nine&quot; seems like it'd make an interesting addition to the World/Chronicles of Darkness. A group of superspies, on the brink of discovering just how deep the rabbit hole goes . . . Seems like it'd be a great story starter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T22:29:14-08:00","id":824829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=824716#post824716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm . . . What era were you thinking, for &quot;Nine&quot;? To be brutally honest . . . they don't really appear to fit any of the core eras. And it seems like they'd be occupying the same &quot;space&quot; as other factions: Project Utopia (the ties to the UN) and the Directive (the espionage angle), for example<br /> <br /> On the other hand, &quot;Nine&quot; seems like it'd make an interesting addition to the World/Chronicles of Darkness. A group of superspies, on the brink of discovering just how deep the rabbit hole goes . . . Seems like it'd be a great story starter</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks to be present-day, the era of the TC corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T04:47:32-08:00","id":824898,"title":"","content":"The core Trinity Continuum rulebook contains a modern-day setting.<br /> <br /> Overlap with the Directive is entirely reasonable, given the hints within the text that 9 will later become the Directive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T08:51:19-08:00","id":824951,"title":"","content":"Actually I'd prefer the Directive to split off from 9. When 9 merges with the U.N. of course it could further split that remains a private corporation.<br /> However I like 9 as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T20:02:37-08:00","id":825212,"title":"","content":"Are we going to have a version of hydra for this game? Perhaps something not so blatantly evil, but definitively nefarious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T01:20:06-08:00","id":825838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=824898#post824898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core Trinity Continuum rulebook contains a modern-day setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm . . . Could you give us a hint at what you're thinking about, timeline-wise? When it came out, <b>Aberrant</b> was set roughly ten years in the future (ca. 2008), and this description of &quot;Nine&quot; seems to pull the &quot;pulp&quot; feel of <b>Adventure</b> dangerously close to the comic book-esque novas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Overlap with the Directive is entirely reasonable, given the hints within the text that 9 will later become the Directive. </div> </div> </div>Two concerns with that. The first might just be a typo, actually. If &quot;Nine&quot; was privatized in the Seventies, then it didn't happen under President Reagan (who was inaugurated in the Eighties). The Seventies were the era of Nixon/Ford/Carter. And, in context, its unlikely Reagan would've gotten rid of such a group - he was a big believer in building up the U.S.'s military and covert intelligence capabilities (Star Wars, Iran-Contra . . . )<br /> <br /> If we're picking a President to privatize the firm . . . maybe Carter, or possibly Bush 41 (as a former CIA director, he could well have had a private feud with the group). However, my money would be on President Clinton, who was a firm believer in the post-Cold War &quot;peace dividend&quot;. <br /> <br /> My second concern involves Nine getting involved with the U.N. Security Council. The five permanent members of the Security Council (US, Great Britain, France, Russia, and China) all have a veto on any proposed policy . . . and there's no way Russia and China are going to be okay with giving an American intelligence agency (even a supposedly privatized one) license to snoop around in their affairs. Maybe, maybe you could bribe/blackmail/frighten China into abstaining (rather than vetoing), but Russia . . . Hell will freeze over, and the Pope will come out as a Taoist, long before Russia even <i>thinks</i> about it. <br /> <br /> Policy-wise, the Putin Regime is deeply concerned (bordering on paranoid) about Western entities expanding into the former Soviet block - Ukraine flirting with joining NATO is often cited as one of the key reasons for the Russian invasion, for example. It also wants to reassert Russian hegemony over the region, seeing the collapse of the Soviet Union as one of the great geopolitical disasters of the 20th Century. And its very fond of using covert actions by the FSB (the re-organized KGB) to suppress dissent (the Polonium poisonings, for example). <br /> <br /> In light of that, there's just no way that the Putin Regime would <i>ever</i> be okay with an American spy agency running loose in their country. And <i>Aberrant </i>is quite clear that Russia is a major backer (and stronghold) of the Directive. . .<br /> <br /> Given the pre-existing dynamics (both real-world and <i>Trinity</i>), the best solution might be to change Nine's country of origin. Off-hand, East Germany's Stasi (secret police) look promising as a parent organization. With the fall of the Berlin Wall, you'd have a lot of highly trained spooks suddenly out of work, with strong ties to Russia, and in need of something else to do with their time. It even sets up some of the friction/paranoia the Directive has towards the (U.S.-based) Aeon Society.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T05:46:28-08:00","id":825937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=825838#post825838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm . . . Could you give us a hint at what you're thinking about, timeline-wise? When it came out, <b>Aberrant</b> was set roughly ten years in the future (ca. 2008), and this description of &quot;Nine&quot; seems to pull the &quot;pulp&quot; feel of <b>Adventure</b> dangerously close to the comic book-esque novas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aberrant is set in 2028.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T14:49:24-08:00","id":827108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=825838#post825838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My second concern involves Nine getting involved with the U.N. Security Council. The five permanent members of the Security Council (US, Great Britain, France, Russia, and China) all have a veto on any proposed policy . . . and there's no way Russia and China are going to be okay with giving an American intelligence agency (even a supposedly privatized one) license to snoop around in their affairs. Maybe, maybe you could bribe/blackmail/frighten China into abstaining (rather than vetoing), but Russia . . . Hell will freeze over, and the Pope will come out as a Taoist, long before Russia even <i>thinks</i> about it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Two things - non-Americans in charge could go a long way. Also if the UN charter happened in the 90s and the Russian oligarchs are well invested, the Yeltsin government would have been way less hostile than the Putin government would be.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm inclined to ignore the Security Council involvement in favor of them being a completely private entity, and just assume the UN charter came with the transformation into the Directive when Russia and China has a uniting concern with the US government (rogue Novas and &quot;Utopia&quot; overturning superpower preeminence).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T14:50:10-08:00","id":827109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=825212#post825212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we going to have a version of hydra for this game? Perhaps something not so blatantly evil, but definitively nefarious?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *looks at Project Proteus*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T18:24:13-08:00","id":827234,"title":"","content":"First Branch 9 was multinational, Russia etc all had the equivalent. While each country had a branch that was the original source of the letters it easily could be argued the other nations folded Branch 9 into their own intelligence and police agencies with the majority of Branch 9 dying during the Second World War or even going rogue all of the Allied governments made deals with various NAZI scientists. The Directive arising from Russia could easily be the Russian version of Branch 9 emerging from the shadows of the NKVD, KGB, FSB and resuming its former role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T10:00:06-08:00","id":828279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=825838#post825838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm . . . Could you give us a hint at what you're thinking about, timeline-wise? When it came out, <b>Aberrant</b> was set roughly ten years in the future (ca. 2008), and this description of &amp;quot;Nine&amp;quot; seems to pull the &amp;quot;pulp&amp;quot; feel of <b>Adventure</b> dangerously close to the comic book-esque novas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that the TC core is going to cover a lot of modern day action-adventure style storytelling, and these days more than a little of that is done with a modern-day pulp-ish or noir-ish aesthetic. It might not be as over the top as 'vintage' pulp can get (&quot;Oh, but you can help us, because I figured out you're secretly the villain's twin brother, but your more athletic build and different hair keep people from spotting it!&quot;), but doing a game in the vein of Leverage or Warehouse 13 is going to come across as very pulp-y regardless of the visual trappings and tech level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T10:11:53-08:00","id":828284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=827108#post827108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I'm inclined to ignore the Security Council involvement in favor of them being a completely private entity, and just assume the UN charter came with the transformation into the Directive when Russia and China has a uniting concern with the US government (rogue Novas and &quot;Utopia&quot; overturning superpower preeminence).</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that it specifically says 9 isn't sure under what circumstances they'd be willing to join up with the UN. Right now they're happy with the status quo, despite the UN's overtures.<br /> <br /> The arrival of novas may be that special circumstance, however, which brings about a change of mind.<br /> <br /> Also of note: until Aberrant comes out, I'm probably going to leave the idea that 9 becomes the Directive fairly ambiguous, as a potential plot hook. Our Aberrant developer may or may not choose to follow with that, and I'm happy with either direction. There are stories to be forged out of the connection (or non-connection) either way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=828279#post828279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that the TC core is going to cover a lot of modern day action-adventure style storytelling, and these days more than a little of that is done with a modern-day pulp-ish or noir-ish aesthetic. It might not be as over the top as 'vintage' pulp can get (&quot;Oh, but you can help us, because I figured out you're secretly the villain's twin brother, but your more athletic build and different hair keep people from spotting it!&quot;), but doing a game in the vein of Leverage or Warehouse 13 is going to come across as very pulp-y regardless of the visual trappings and tech level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nailed it.<br /> <br /> As with anything, there are dials to be tuned. You can keep things weird in the vein of Eureka where, if not a monster-of-the-week, there's at least a new fairly bizarre circumstance happening with regularity. Or you can keep things fairly grounded, like with Leverage, where they go up against corrupt CEOs and politicians. Or maybe you want to go somewhere in between, like with Stargate SG-1 (which, I may remind, begins with the Stargate being found in Egypt in the 1920s), where the circumstances are weird (aliens and distant worlds) but it's at least the same general sort of situation every episode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T10:29:39-08:00","id":828288,"title":"","content":"Next up, Les Fantomes: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-les-fantomes-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-le...ity-continuum/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T19:14:55-08:00","id":828547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=828284#post828284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that it specifically says 9 isn't sure under what circumstances they'd be willing to join up with the UN. Right now they're happy with the status quo, despite the UN's overtures.<br /> <br /> The arrival of novas may be that special circumstance, however, which brings about a change of mind.<br /> <br /> Also of note: until Aberrant comes out, I'm probably going to leave the idea that 9 becomes the Directive fairly ambiguous, as a potential plot hook. Our Aberrant developer may or may not choose to follow with that, and I'm happy with either direction. There are stories to be forged out of the connection (or non-connection) either way. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with <b>GlamourWeaver</b>. For lack of a better term, the UN isn't &quot;effective&quot; (or maybe &quot;organizationally healthy&quot;) enough, to conduct that kind of outreach. The Aeon Society's approach - actively lobbying, coupled with a <i>massive</i> backdoor bribe - is probably the only way to get an effective UN-sponsored team in the field. Just look at how much they hamstring their peacekeeping forces, in the real world.<br /> <br /> If you want Nine to be approached by a trans-national entity, why not use Interpol? It would make sense that they'd need a division/group devoted to the &quot;weird&quot; stuff, and Interpol itself was cited as a direct example of the sort of organization the founders wanted, when setting up the Directive. Interpol has the right institutional &quot;feel&quot; for Nine, too.<br /> <br /> (Going with Interpol also helps keeping Nine from infringing on the future turf of Project Utopia, which becomes a part of the UN during the <i>Aberrant</i> era).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T20:10:04-08:00","id":828570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=828288#post828288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next up, Les Fantomes: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-les-fantomes-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-le...ity-continuum/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Looks promising - I can definitely see &quot;Les Fantomes&quot; in a super-spy/gentlemen-thief type game. One brief note, though - are you sure you want to explicitly name the head of their group? Seems like a group like that would have more of an amorphous structure, and would try to hide the leadership (to the point that even some of the membership might not know who is calling the shots). Personally, I'd be tempted to make Sabine Durant the flamboyant spokeswoman for the group, and leave it an open question whether she's also the boss.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: Oh, and one other thing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> such as a prototype near-zero emission engine returned to the Triton Foundation </div> </div> </div>Weren't the &quot;super&quot; engines/reactors invented by novas, during the <i>Aberrant</i> era? Or are they being retconned into the modern day setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 02-11-2016, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T23:29:28-08:00","id":828622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=828547#post828547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with <b>GlamourWeaver</b>. For lack of a better term, the UN isn't &quot;effective&quot; (or maybe &quot;organizationally healthy&quot;) enough, to conduct that kind of outreach.</div> </div> </div> </div>The UN in the Trinity Universe is and has always been a different sort of thing than the one we have in the real world. A close friend of mine actually majored in International Relations and sees no issue whatsoever with the way I laid things out, given the differences between Trinity!UN with real!UN. Particularly given the existence of organizations like Doctor Who's UNIT, No One Lives Forever's UNITY, and The Man From UNCLE's UNCLE in the action-adventure genre, it's clear the purview of the Trinity!UN is a wee bit wider than the one we'd ordinarily expect.<br /> <br /> I've also been directed to point out <a href=\"http://ptx.sagepub.com/content/36/4/607.full.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Sovereignty and the UFO</a> and its application to the emergence of novas on the UN.<br /> <br /> So I'm satisfied with the existing explanation. Feel free to change it if you like, but this is the universe of the Trinity Continuum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Going with Interpol also helps keeping Nine from infringing on the future turf of Project Utopia, which becomes a part of the UN during the <i>Aberrant</i> era). </div> </div> </div>There can be countless organizations tied to the US government, but more than one associated with the UN is &quot;infringing on their turf&quot;? The two organizations and their (potential) UN connections are <i>very</i> different beasts. You may certainly do things differently in your games if you prefer, but I don't see the big overlap problem you're seeing. It's the rough equivalent of the US Senate letting the United Way sit in on sessions while simultaneous employing Blackwater to do dirty work. They're very different organizations who do very different things and their associations with the government are very different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 02-12-2016, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T23:31:34-08:00","id":828623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=828570#post828570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't the &quot;super&quot; engines/reactors invented by novas, during the <i>Aberrant</i> era? Or are they being retconned into the modern day setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Near zero emission engine&quot; is a very different thing from &quot;fusion engine.&quot;<br /> <br /> The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ZENN\" target=\"_blank\">ZENN car</a> (Zero Emissions, No Noise) is an electric car which is available right now in the present.<br /> <br /> Fusion-powered cars are not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T23:17:37-08:00","id":829144,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with Sabine Durant being openly the leader of the Fantomes. That seems to be normal for the genre, as far as I can tell, because it just sells the character is that good that the cops know who they are and still can't catch the fucker. Carmen San Diego and Lupin III are both very much leaders of their respected gangs, and the police of their universes know this...it hasn't made either character more easily caught.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T12:04:34-08:00","id":832644,"title":"","content":"This week, we have the Theseus Club. <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-the-theseus-club-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-th...ity-continuum/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T15:05:01-08:00","id":832780,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna wreck so many Nazis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T15:09:02-08:00","id":832784,"title":"","content":"I hope you guys put some space between the kickstarter's I dont want to have to choose between this or scion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T16:17:54-08:00","id":832814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=832780#post832780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna wreck so many Nazis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pfft. The Nazis were defeated in World War II.<br /> <br /> ... and least, the Nazis occupying the <i>surface world</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she