ve a faction from the Dark Side?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T09:21:44-08:00","id":833872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=833718#post833718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the impression Scion is further along that Trinity, but I may be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit of a race, but one we both win, since playtests of one that affect core systems will affect the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T19:25:02-08:00","id":834190,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to see the design of two fairly different games have so much cross influence on each other. The final product promises to be fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T06:57:54-08:00","id":835002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=834190#post834190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting to see the design of two fairly different games have so much cross influence on each other. The final product promises to be fascinating.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the start, I noted that Trinity and Scion share some of the same needs, the same media inspirations (pulp -&gt; action thriller -&gt; superheroes -&gt; operatic drama). The idea that they share a base system isn't a bad one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T05:51:55-08:00","id":835693,"title":"","content":"So, could you start a game using the main system and turn it into a Scion or Aberrant game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T09:11:55-08:00","id":835819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=835693#post835693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, could you start a game using the main system and turn it into a Scion or Aberrant game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Trinity and Scion both use proprietary variants of Storypath, so, no. But there will probably be some similar assumptions.<br /> <br /> At this stage, without both systems having been fully built, I guess I'd ballpark it at playing a cWoD Werewolf in a cWoD Vampire game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T09:15:33-08:00","id":835820,"title":"","content":"My main question is this: Does belonging to an allegiance provide any mechanical bonusses? and if so, are there going to be rules to build your own allegiances?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T09:15:50-08:00","id":835822,"title":"","content":"Right. Ultimately the core of both games is the same, but the details differ enough that it wouldn't be a seamless transition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T09:17:22-08:00","id":835824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=835820#post835820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main question is this: Does belonging to an allegiance provide any mechanical bonusses? and if so, are there going to be rules to build your own allegiances?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes and maybe. Rules wouldn't be much more involved than &quot;look at what we made and use that as a template for your own&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T09:53:24-08:00","id":835847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=835824#post835824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and maybe. Rules wouldn't be much more involved than &quot;look at what we made and use that as a template for your own&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand on what Ian said:<br /> <br /> Building your own Allegiance or Path isn't hard to do (and is, in fact, encouraged). It's actually pretty easy to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T12:45:51-08:00","id":835944,"title":"","content":"Cool organizations for spy game. They just read too much like a splat options to me, rather than organizations which imo defeat the whole purpose of Paths themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T10:36:10-08:00","id":837080,"title":"","content":"The latest teaser from John Snead:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-the-transcendent-alliance-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-the-transcendent-alliance-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\"> Allegiance: The Transcendent Alliance [Trinity Continuum] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-the-transcendent-alliance-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-the-transcendent-alliance-trinity-continuum/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T16:38:06-08:00","id":837285,"title":"","content":"I want to play an anti-eugenicist trans humanist who goes on a holy war to purge his faction of eugenicists!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T17:32:07-08:00","id":837311,"title":"","content":"Perfectly valid!<br /> <br /> The Allegiances obviously have quite a bit of variation; many of them can be used as either protagonist or antagonist factions, or even both at the same time. That's intentional. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just using the MCU as an example, Howard Stark, Tony Stark, and Samuel Stearns would all fit as members of the Transcendent Alliance, but so would the Red Skull, Dr. Zola, Werner Reinhardt/Daniel Whitehall, and the Centipede Group. Bruce Banner may have started off as one, but got disillusioned once he found out what was &quot;really&quot; going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 02-25-2016, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T20:46:54-08:00","id":837380,"title":"","content":"In TC lore, I'm guessing that the Transcendent Alliance is what Dr. Primorius is up to in the Action timeframe; and that barring interference, it's the Allegiance that's likely to trigger the Aberrant setting. Assuming that he's still part of TC's lore, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T00:40:58-08:00","id":837424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=837285#post837285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to play an anti-eugenicist trans humanist who goes on a holy war to purge his faction of eugenicists!</div> </div> </div> </div>*beating a crypto-fascist in the face*<br /> <br /> IDI<br /> *smash*<br /> OCRACY<br /> *smash*<br /> IS<br /> *smash*<br /> NOT<br /> *smash*<br /> A<br /> *smash*<br /> GOOD<br /> *smash*<br /> MOVIE!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T02:18:10-08:00","id":837447,"title":"","content":"So if the Leadership ties into the meta plot we're already familiar with... It's either Michael or the Doyen. Either would make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T19:31:13-08:00","id":837870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=837447#post837447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if the Leadership ties into the meta plot we're already familiar with... It's either Michael or the Doyen. Either would make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Mercer I don't like Max never have and while I understand those that do if we tie to the existing overall plot I could see a sidebar using all three as possible founders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-26T21:10:02-08:00","id":837914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=837870#post837870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or Mercer I don't like Max never have and while I understand those that do if we tie to the existing overall plot I could see a sidebar using all three as possible founders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Engineered human transcendence is kind of against Mercer's core ethos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T22:23:08-08:00","id":838473,"title":"","content":"One thing I like about these previews is that aside from the Triton Foundation, every Allegiance we've seen so far has a dark side, even if they have noble goals.<br /> <br /> 9 can be SHIELD, but they're ultimately privatized government spooks preserving the status quo. Les Fantomes can play Robin Hood as much as they want, but at the end of the day, they're still just a bunch of crooks and thieves. The Theseus Club employs individuals of questionable background (see the Yakuza board member), and is perfectly willing to throw due process out the window in pursuit of their prey. Then there's the Transcendent Alliance, who refuses to commit atrocities, but is totally okay with profiting from someone <i>else's</i> atrocities.<br /> <br /> A lot of moral gray here; plenty of plot fodder and story-role flexibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:37:20-08:00","id":838505,"title":"","content":"Excellent observation! I didn't want to have a section where <i>these</i> are the protagonist groups and <i>these</i> are the antagonists. Some are better or worse than others, but you should be able to run some really good stories featuring just the groups presented, whether you choose to use them as protags or antags or both. Uprooting the negative elements of your own group is a well-worn trope with a lot of variations ranging from betrayal, to all-out civil war, to a single bad apple. Season to taste.<br /> <br /> (Also, the Triton teaser I posted last October wasn't the full writeup on them, so you have that to look forward to.)<br /> <br /> I'd like to point out that the built-in good/evil dichotomy isn't something I specifically requested of my writers; they all just nailed it naturally. They've all delivered some stellar material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T00:03:46-08:00","id":838516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=838505#post838505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent observation! I didn't want to have a section where <i>these</i> are the protagonist groups and <i>these</i> are the antagonists. Some are better or worse than others, but you should be able to run some really good stories featuring just the groups presented, whether you choose to use them as protags or antags or both. Uprooting the negative elements of your own group is a well-worn trope with a lot of variations ranging from betrayal, to all-out civil war, to a single bad apple. Season to taste.<br /> <br /> (Also, the Triton teaser I posted last October wasn't the full writeup on them, so you have that to look forward to.)<br /> <br /> I'd like to point out that the built-in good/evil dichotomy isn't something I specifically requested of my writers; they all just nailed it naturally. They've all delivered some stellar material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am <i>very</i> interested in seeing what the Aeon society's moral gray area looks like. I believe in <i>Adventure!</i> Mercer explicitly tells his recruits that in order to maintain good will, they don't go anywhere they aren't invited. Which means that Aeon's opponents can get away with <i>a lot</i> of bad things, as long as they convince the local &quot;legitimate&quot; authorities to wave the Society off and silence all other voices.<br /> <br /> That also raises an interesting question of what precisely constitutes a legitimate call for help. Will the Society back off from helping the common people if the government tells them to leave? Will they aid private individuals against the public will and opinion if the individual's goals and methods align with Aeon's ideals? Who decides which calls for aid to answer or ignore, and why?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T01:54:06-08:00","id":838543,"title":"","content":"Is a Triton a full Allegiance in its own right separate from the Aeon Society?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T06:54:09-08:00","id":838620,"title":"","content":"I have always said that being a good person depends on the player, not the organization they belong to. Morality is a personal thing. Organizations can favour certain moral inclinations, but they should never be monolitic about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T07:55:31-08:00","id":838640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=838543#post838543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a Triton a full Allegiance in its own right separate from the Aeon Society?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how to answer this, because the Aeon Society is not written up as an Allegiance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T09:15:09-08:00","id":838669,"title":"","content":"Interesting group . . . My guess is that the Transcendent Alliance will fracture after N-Day, with various members eventually joining Project Proteus, various Japanese corporations, and the Teragen's Harvester faction. All of whom are willing to turn a blind eye to ethical concerns, and/or push the limits of science.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=838516#post838516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am <i>very</i> interested in seeing what the Aeon society's moral gray area looks like. I believe in <i>Adventure!</i> Mercer explicitly tells his recruits that in order to maintain good will, they don't go anywhere they aren't invited. Which means that Aeon's opponents can get away with <i>a lot</i> of bad things, as long as they convince the local &quot;legitimate&quot; authorities to wave the Society off and silence all other voices.<br /> <br /> That also raises an interesting question of what precisely constitutes a legitimate call for help. Will the Society back off from helping the common people if the government tells them to leave? Will they aid private individuals against the public will and opinion if the individual's goals and methods align with Aeon's ideals? Who decides which calls for aid to answer or ignore, and why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on notes from the old <b>Aberrant</b> game, the flaw in Aeon is a mix of paternalism and being blinded by their own shining ideals. Despite Mercer's original intentions, by the 1970s or so, the upper echelon of Aeon is convinced that humanity &quot;needs&quot; them, and their guidance . . .and will always need them. And they're prepared to do whatever is &quot;best&quot; for humanity, no matter what.<br /> <br /> &quot;For the Greater Good&quot; . . . so much evil is possible, when you start thinking that way. There was a diary entry in the . . .<i> Player's Guide</i> (?), written long before Project Proteus kicks off, where one of the founding members expresses his horror and disgust after Aeon's board approves a permanent division devoted to intrigue, dirty tricks, and wetwork (i.e. killing people)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T12:00:37-08:00","id":838737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=838640#post838640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure how to answer this, because the Aeon Society is not written up as an Allegiance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really!? I just assumed they would be the generic do-gooder allegiance like they were in (first edition) Adventure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T12:14:49-08:00","id":838744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=838737#post838737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really!? I just assumed they would be the generic do-gooder allegiance like they were in (first edition) Adventure!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is close to the Aberrant era, so keep in mind that Aeon is far bigger than it was back in the Adventure! era. So you've already got stuff like Project Pandora, Project Tantalus, the Triton Foundation, and similar organizations from Aberrant. Aeon certainly exists, but you're more likely as a Talent to have an Allegiance in one of its various arms, because that's where the action is happening on a day-to-day basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T15:04:50-08:00","id":838823,"title":"","content":"So would Novas and Psions also be connected to these allegiances or are they more geared towards other things?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T15:15:25-08:00","id":838825,"title":"","content":"The TC rulebook contains the modern-day setting and rules for Talents (daredevils). Psions are found in Aeon, and Novas are found in Aberrant. So no, the Allegiances in the core are not geared toward other types of Inspired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T18:44:05-08:00","id":838900,"title":"","content":"Will Adventure! era Mesmerists and Stalwarts get there own rules? They were pretty thematically different in terms of their powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T21:58:28-08:00","id":838964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=838900#post838900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Adventure! era Mesmerists and Stalwarts get there own rules? They were pretty thematically different in terms of their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to make any definitive comments at this point on books that are that far down the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T22:35:46-08:00","id":838979,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T15:01:08-08:00","id":841520,"title":"","content":"Craig Oxbrow brings us The Neptune Foundation: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-neptune-foundation-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-ne...ity-continuum/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T15:17:20-08:00","id":841526,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I'm a little unclear what the narrative value of the separate Neptune and Triton Foundation options are from a player perspective, compared to just having one of the game's core Allegiances be &quot;nonprofit disaster-relief and medical response/aid&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T15:31:10-08:00","id":841535,"title":"","content":"Neptune was admittedly a bit of a late addition, I think the last Allegiance written up, although it's something I wanted in there from the beginning. Triton is more about long-term goals, exploration, and research, while Neptune is more focused on short-term emergencies and disaster relief. In broad strokes, Triton figures out the problems, Neptune solves them.<br /> <br /> As always, the material you're seeing isn't even full first draft form. I'm not giving you a peak into anything remotely complete, because it doesn't exist yet. Descriptions of Foundations will be tweaked in later drafts to highlight their differences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T19:08:59-08:00","id":841652,"title":"","content":"Can I just say how much I adore the fact that Neptune is basically realistic-yet-still-optimistic-Thunderbirds? Because that sounds <i>wonderful</i>. These guys have their own TV show in-universe don't they? Of course they do, I don't know why I asked.<br /> <br /> I'm <i>loving</i> this optimistic turn from Onyx Path. Genuine heroism FTW!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T19:17:23-08:00","id":841656,"title":"","content":"I guess I'll have to see a longer write up for Triton, because now I'm not clear on what kind of adventures Triton PCs have, as this was the type of stuff I was imagining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T19:23:26-08:00","id":841658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=841652#post841652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I just say how much I adore the fact that Neptune is basically realistic-yet-still-optimistic-Thunderbirds? Because that sounds <i>wonderful</i>. These guys have their own TV show in-universe don't they? Of course they do, I don't know why I asked.<br /> <br /> I'm <i>loving</i> this optimistic turn from Onyx Path. Genuine heroism FTW!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Filmed in <i>Ultramannequination</i>!<br /> <br /> My own inspiration for Neptune was (as might be guessed from the screenshot heading the article) the <i>Phoenix Foundation</i> from MacGyver, and to a lesser extend the Foundation for Law And Government (FLAGG, later the Knight Foundation) of <i>Knight Rider</i>. Mac is basically a one-man First Response team, although he does frequently work with others. And he is absolutely a Talent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T00:08:29-08:00","id":841763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=841535#post841535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neptune was admittedly a bit of a late addition, I think the last Allegiance written up, although it's something I wanted in there from the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>About how many Allegiances are there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T00:26:54-08:00","id":841770,"title":"","content":"Right now, I have 17 Allegiance writeups of various lengths. I might trim one or two of them out for space, but anything I don't use in the core will almost certainly get used somewhere else down the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T22:25:01-08:00","id":842413,"title":"","content":"Sounds reasonable.<br /> <br /> So far Allegiances seem to be fairly specific - that is, they don't seem to be things that seem so obvious the player could just come up with them on their own, so there is both room for tailoring ones own and yet the official Allegiances still provide plenty of coverage.<br /> <br /> The only thing I worry about right off hand is Allegiances working out to be like the Compacts and Conspiracies in Hunter: the Vigil - given a very brief treatment that really demands to be fully fleshed out, but then never really touched on again and fairly easily forgotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T09:38:22-08:00","id":842610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=842413#post842413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds reasonable.<br /> <br /> So far Allegiances seem to be fairly specific - that is, they don't seem to be things that seem so obvious the player could just come up with them on their own, so there is both room for tailoring ones own and yet the official Allegiances still provide plenty of coverage.<br /> <br /> The only thing I worry about right off hand is Allegiances working out to be like the Compacts and Conspiracies in Hunter: the Vigil - given a very brief treatment that really demands to be fully fleshed out, but then never really touched on again and fairly easily forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>This brings to my head an important question. Are there going to be supplements for the setting of the corebook?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T13:21:25-08:00","id":843116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=842610#post842610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This brings to my head an important question. Are there going to be supplements for the setting of the corebook?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scion is being quoted as being open-ended; presumably that means similar for Trinity Continuum. They also seem to be following in the footsteps of Chronicles of Darkness, and several of the source books for that games core book setting are some of the best supplements for the entire setting overall.<br /> <br /> Notably, we don't have to go back to the splat-book days of things. It's perfectly possible to say, print one big book that gives all the allegiances extra details, history and the like, although maybe we would want to split that into a few books of related Allegiances if we are going to have as many as mentioned earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T20:27:43-08:00","id":843274,"title":"","content":"The Trinity Continuum rulebook mostly contains <i>hints </i>of a modern-day setting. Via the artifacts (newspaper clippings, audio transcripts, internal memos, etc.) at the beginning of the book, and the Allegiances near the end. By showing you some Allegiances available to use, I'm showing you the types of stories I feel fit within the Continuum and that I expect people will end up playing. Often writeups mention several other organizations which aren't covered in the Allegiance section. That's intentional: I want this world to feel full of danger and secrets and adventure, but I'm not going to fill in all of those blanks for you.<br /> <br /> So to make a long story short, while I have a number of supplements planned, they're similar to the CofD blue books. They expand on the capabilities of the line by treading new territory. I don't <i>currently</i> have any plans to go into more detail on the core's Allegiances. I'd rather create new ones (and a big book about Aeon would probably be better served as an Aberrant book). But that's not to say books going into further detail about Allegiances won't ever happen. They'd make good fodder for Kickstarter stretch goals, for example.<br /> <br /> I think we'll get the book out there first and let people play around with them and see what ideas people grab on to and what they don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T23:04:26-08:00","id":843304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=842413#post842413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds reasonable.<br /> <br /> So far Allegiances seem to be fairly specific - that is, they don't seem to be things that seem so obvious the player could just come up with them on their own, so there is both room for tailoring ones own and yet the official Allegiances still provide plenty of coverage.<br /> <br /> The only thing I worry about right off hand is Allegiances working out to be like the Compacts and Conspiracies in Hunter: the Vigil - given a very brief treatment that really demands to be fully fleshed out, but then never really touched on again and fairly easily forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the need to point out that the core 12 C&amp;C are expanded on in literally every single HtV supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T11:30:54-08:00","id":843535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=843274#post843274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Trinity Continuum rulebook mostly contains <i>hints </i>of a modern-day setting. Via the artifacts (newspaper clippings, audio transcripts, internal memos, etc.) at the beginning of the book, and the Allegiances near the end. By showing you some Allegiances available to use, I'm showing you the types of stories I feel fit within the Continuum and that I expect people will end up playing. Often writeups mention several other organizations which aren't covered in the Allegiance section. That's intentional: I want this world to feel full of danger and secrets and adventure, but I'm not going to fill in all of those blanks for you.<br /> <br /> So to make a long story short, while I have a number of supplements planned, they're similar to the CofD blue books. They expand on the capabilities of the line by treading new territory. I don't <i>currently</i> have any plans to go into more detail on the core's Allegiances. I'd rather create new ones (and a big book about Aeon would probably be better served as an Aberrant book). But that's not to say books going into further detail about Allegiances won't ever happen. They'd make good fodder for Kickstarter stretch goals, for example.<br /> <br /> I think we'll get the book out there first and let people play around with them and see what ideas people grab on to and what they don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will you introduce versions of these organizations in the other lines? Maybe not with a full entry, but perhaps as a sidebar that indicates what form they adopt in that era?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T19:59:44-08:00","id":843762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=843304#post843304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel the need to point out that the core 12 C&amp;C are expanded on in literally every single HtV supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Union thinks vampires are bad&quot; is not really my idea of fleshing out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T00:28:03-08:00","id":843849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=843762#post843762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;The Union thinks vampires are bad&quot; is not really my idea of fleshing out.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were in-setting documents for every single group, plot hooks, strategies, history for the older groups, Endowments for the Conspiracies...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-08T10:51:11-08:00","id":844046,"title":"","content":"If you guys want to argue the relative merits of Hunter supplements, please take it to a different thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T19:21:18-08:00","id":844867,"title":"","content":"I was going to say we were getting off topic...<br /> So anyway, that gives us <i>three</i> potential set-ups: A) Write-up and then basically ignore B) Individual Books (C Touched on in each supplement. I favor B, it sounds like they are going with A.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T23:44:52-08:00","id":1059966,"title":"","content":"Pulling this back up with <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-archangel-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">the new preview for Archangel</a>, featuring the family of an old Aberrant favorite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T08:54:19-08:00","id":1060115,"title":"","content":"Is Allegiance the Modern Time Period for Aeon or is it like 90's or turn of the Century/Millenium?<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh it is modern, and its going to be in the Corebook? So is the Corebook called Allegiance? Coolsville. Very Excited about Aeon being a Thing! I missed the boat last time!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","user":"Eldagusto","date":". 03-08-2017, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T10:02:59-08:00","id":1060151,"title":"","content":"It took me a minute to figure out what you were asking.<br /> <br /> No, &quot;Allegiance&quot; is not the name of any era. An allegiance is a group or organization to which you belong, as seen here on the original character sheets for Trinity, Aberrant, and Adventure!:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/QEtQczW.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/QEtQczW.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/QEtQczW.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://i.imgur.com/QEtQczW.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T10:03:59-08:00","id":1060152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/824274-allegiance-previews?p=1060115#post1060115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Allegiance the Modern Time Period for Aeon or is it like 90's or turn of the Century/Millenium?<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh it is modern, and its going to be in the Corebook? So is the Corebook called Allegiance? Coolsville. Very Excited about Aeon being a Thing! I missed the boat last time!</div> </div> </div> </div>Allegiance isn't the corebook's name; it's used to indicate this is a group you can belong to. Like Tribe, Tradition, Covenant, etc.<br /> <br /> Earlier previewed Allegiances:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/day-15-aberrant-splitting-time-like-a-trident/\" target=\"_blank\">Triton Foundation</a> (partial writeup in the bottom of the post)<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-9-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">9</a><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-les-fantomes-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">Les Fant\u00f4mes</a><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-the-theseus-club-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">Theseus Club</a><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-the-transcendent-alliance-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">Transcendant Alliance</a><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/allegiance-neptune-foundation-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">Neptune Foundation</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T17:23:18-08:00","id":1060346,"title":"","content":"Wait so the Book the Most Dangerous Game describes events that actually happened in the Aeoniverse?! Why do they get a direct port, like Promethean got Frankenstein, and Vampire got Dracula. But we are assuming say Doc Savage isn't a specific character that existed, but characters similar to him have, but Zaroff totally existed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T17:28:15-08:00","id":1060347,"title":"","content":"Ooooh :P!<br /> <br /> Sorry I am new to Trinity. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"dat